    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TO_0000112 -->

    <Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TO_0000112">
        <rdfs:label>microbial disease response</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TO_0000179"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>disease resistance trait (narrow)</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>disease control (broad)</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>plant_trait_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <rdfs:comment>The plant response to a microbial infection may be manifested in either the whole plant (PO:0000003) or in parts of the plant. The damage is a direct measure of resistance to the particular pathogen causing the disease.</rdfs:comment>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>disease susceptibility (narrow)</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>TO:0000112</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>disease tolerance (narrow)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <ns3:IAO_0000115>A biotic plant stress trait (TO:0000179) which is the response to damage to a plant structure (PO:0009011) caused by an infection by a microbial pathogen.</ns3:IAO_0000115>
    </Class>
    


